7592186415898 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415908 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415913 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415923 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1077 "selection" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415898 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415935 1079 #uuid "e4962c93-3582-5793-94a8-d5e64919a899" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415936 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415935 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415936 1069 "q-161183" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415936 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415936 1071 "Find the surface area of the portion of the surface $z=\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by $y=\\sqrt{1+4x}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=2.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415936 1072 #uuid "0071fbbf-507b-5e86-9e07-511fe6080666" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415936 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1+4x}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/9a/9a459a9807befc312528771626dca293a7ebbccd97a2c1e938f47a2d90a36726.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3})=2\\sqrt{x}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3})=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(2\\sqrt{x})}^{2}+(0)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1+4x}}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{1+4x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(1+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x+2{x}^{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(2+8)-0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415937 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415934 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415937 1069 "q-109765" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415937 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415937 1071 "Find the surface area of the part of the surface $z=xy$ that is subject to the constraint ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415937 1072 #uuid "139ae790-9731-55fc-ab5e-266ae6726353" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415937 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=xy,\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f0/f0faa92e0f89c86248abffad7f61cac5d94a3848a7f7be4464c4b28d3915aa32.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(y)^{2}+(x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=1+{r}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=2r\\,\\text{d}r.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {[\\frac{2}{3}\\,{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{[{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}[{2}^{3/2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi (2\\sqrt{2}-1)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415938 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415930 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415938 1069 "q-161442" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415938 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415938 1071 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(x,z)\\,:\\,\\boxed{}\\,}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the part of the cone $y=4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ that lies inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$ From left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415938 1072 #uuid "1d2fc887-f2a2-5a12-af93-46ac7487f8f4" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415938 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}},\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}})=\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}})=\\frac{4z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{4z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}+\\frac{16{z}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{17({x}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$\\,$ $\\sqrt{17}\\,$ and $\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415939 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415933 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415939 1069 "q-161175" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415939 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415939 1071 "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $y=3x+2z$ that is subject to the constraints ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 16,\\,x\\le 0$ and $z\\ge 0.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415939 1072 #uuid "3a9f44f1-362f-50d2-bbcf-0383dfbcd3ea" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415939 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=3x+2z,\\,(x,z)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 16,\\,x\\le 0,\\,z\\ge 0},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/48/48ffe2b0bd40937205d9b9d3b6cc264f83bd56ea30a5df318ba7c7507efb68f7.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+2z)=3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x+2z)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+9+4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{14}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot [\\theta ]_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =4\\pi \\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415940 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415932 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415940 1069 "q-161129" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415940 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415940 1071 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of $z=3{x}^{2}-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415940 1072 #uuid "795a5978-6945-51dd-9230-522e60fb9dd8" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415940 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=3{x}^{2}-y,\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-y)=6x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y)=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(6x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+36{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415941 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415928 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415941 1069 "q-161226" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415941 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415941 1071 "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $x=\\frac{y-z}{3}$ whose projection onto the $yz$-plane is bounded by the constraints $1\\le y\\le 4$ and $1\\le z\\le 3.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415941 1072 #uuid "b3090cbd-55f4-50b9-b96a-e12ca57ae315" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415941 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{y-z}{3},\\,(y,z)\\in D,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,1\\le z\\le 3},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f06a9c686a935cb6c561affbcd224045618d9cacaf94eb7c9eab8a9ca8da44c.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y-z}{3})=\\frac{1}{3}, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{y-z}{3})=-\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{9}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot (3-1) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415942 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415931 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415942 1069 "q-161153" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415942 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415942 1071 "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $z=2\\sqrt{5}x+2y$ that is bounded by the constraints $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415942 1072 #uuid "e0057193-1fc8-5f60-b2e8-92515ea3b1e6" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true] [17592186415942 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{5}x+2y,\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\sqrt{5}x+2y)=2\\sqrt{5}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{5}x+2y)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+20+4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{25}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (1-(-1))\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534249 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-03199862-16b9-557b-8bef-764c1954ae8a" 17592186415888 "answer-0d1c8e0a-12da-57b1-b178-119e2ed0094c" 17592186415889 "answer-134a8ec5-3c99-5a35-b135-9550a1a589e4" 17592186415890 "answer-1735e166-5acc-5324-851d-91faeb7a9618" 17592186415891 "answer-1aa6f07d-e7c8-523d-bd08-943563edb16a" 17592186415892 "answer-1b05d304-e890-5571-a95a-08cab23c0431" 17592186415893 "answer-26f6af28-58a5-5980-8be5-d39c9b4b3514" 17592186415894 "answer-3369dcb6-e91a-5e4b-b5d1-596236417674" 17592186415895 "answer-3a4ce4b5-b090-52fb-8521-91a7d5fb6e64" 17592186415896 "answer-3dc37952-1697-5509-8bc7-6ccd85ec6880" 17592186415897 "answer-3f58fbfa-2a3c-5f8a-8c15-ac63c162c8c4" 17592186415898 "answer-4281a994-2dee-5d00-a661-565bf6f7aacd" 17592186415899 "answer-4ba101ca-c17d-55ee-8ca8-392a0b3b4fd5" 17592186415900 "answer-5269f1b8-3177-521a-9c3f-e7af2b0e1033" 17592186415901 "answer-543c20d4-2012-58fc-988d-4183a7a0d1bb" 17592186415902 "answer-5c5b7aca-0852-5446-be6b-4b27132d1d3a" 17592186415903 "answer-7853d8da-02ca-52fe-82ab-8d3e95436d1c" 17592186415904 "answer-89d97de7-0a07-5bd0-a64a-ce2c1b74eb86" 17592186415905 "answer-944324b3-9b00-578a-a869-20197fc9cd6b" 17592186415906 "answer-96e2a9a0-2d62-5a79-a93d-b7db07b18154" 17592186415907 "answer-9c2e9088-2863-5032-aa2c-88ec65760072" 17592186415908 "answer-a1ae44f3-7378-59c0-9c18-c2dc952a1624" 17592186415909 "answer-a7727358-0e8f-5186-a4f4-a4093c7f5305" 17592186415910 "answer-aea19d27-cea1-5633-a35f-860030bc1eeb" 17592186415911 "answer-b4f9a248-c377-505f-ac3a-9e96059ce3f5" 17592186415912